# One anypoint view out of a fisheye image, rendered by the Moildev SDK port.
#
# Used by Center Setup and by the 3D dialog. Both of them used to hold a Moildev
# instance in the client and build the dense per-pixel remap themselves -- which
# is a 3040x3040 coordinate transform, i.e. exactly the kind of work that is not
# supposed to happen on a remote any more.
#
# The remap tables are cached on the server per (source, camera, direction,
# angles, zoom, mode). Re-asking for the same view is a lookup and an encode;
# only a change of angle rebuilds anything.

# Which loaded source to draw from -- see Measure3dSource.srv. Use "capture" for
# the frame the camera last returned, which is what Center Setup wants.
string source_id

# Camera parameter JSON (the *_params.json the operator picks). May be empty when
# source_id already carries its parameters.
string params_json

# alpha, beta, theta in degrees, then the zoom factor.
float64 alpha
float64 beta
float64 theta
float64 zoom

# 1 or 2 -- the Moildev anypoint mode. Mode 2 is the dense per-pixel transform.
int32 mode

# Camera name inside params_json, when it holds several. Empty for the first.
string camera_type

# Working resolution ratio. 1.0 is the file's own calibration resolution; Center
# Setup drops it for a faster preview on large sensors.
float64 resolution_ratio

# Override the optical centre, so the view follows Center Setup's spin boxes.
# has_center false uses the file's own icx/icy.
bool has_center
int32 icx
int32 icy

# Output size. 0 x 0 keeps the source's size.
int32 width
int32 height

# Shrink the returned copy only. 0 for none.
int32 max_side
---
bool success
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage image
int32 width
int32 height
string message
